.TH GENESIS-HEARING 7 "October 2026" "Genesis 0.2.0" "Genesis Manual"
.SH NAME
genesis-hearing \- the auditory faculties: ambient listening and the auditory cortex
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBoccipital_lobe.perception.ambient\fR  the streaming listener (Vosk STT)
\fBtemporal_lobe.auditory\fR            the auditory cortex for non-speech sound
\fBtemporal_lobe.speech\fR              VoiceInput single-utterance STT
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Genesis has two ears. One listens for words: the ambient listener
captures microphone audio continuously, transcribes with Vosk
(offline), and emits complete utterances \(em it does not decide
whether to respond; wake-word detection ("genesis" addresses her)
and the choice to chime in on a topic she has context on are the
caller's. The other ear hears everything else.
.SS The auditory cortex
.I temporal_lobe/auditory.py
captures audio on a background thread, computes spectral features in
real time, and classifies sound events \(em silence below the energy
floor, music (tonal, sustained, regular rhythm), impacts (sudden
onset, high energy, short duration \(em door slam, clap, bark), and
ambient noise \(em so the room's non-speech texture reaches her:
depth, loudness, tonality, and brevity in the reports that surface
in conversation.
.SS Voice input
.IR temporal_lobe/speech.py 's
.I VoiceInput
is the blocking single-utterance path behind
.BR /voice ,
for an addressed exchange rather than the always-on stream.
.B /voice-mode
holds continuous voice conversation.
.SS The other ear
A separate afferent listens outward rather than into the room:
.BR genesis-discord (7)
documents the bot-token ear that hears her channel.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B /voice
Speak to Genesis (one utterance).
.TP
.B /voice-mode
Continuous voice conversation.
